# UX Architect

Turn `prd/niscorp-company-site.md` into a layout a developer can build. Do not add a second design system or a theme toggle.

## Information architecture

Follow the routes in `prd/niscorp-company-site.md`. Home links to the three offers. AI and websites link to Contact. Enterprise is a section on Services and links to Contact. Header and footer on every page. The header Services control is a disclosure. The footer is the four-column row in the PRD. Phone, email, and WhatsApp stay in the contact actions, with one shared card style. A floating WhatsApp button sits on every page.

Home order: hero with the three cards, trust strip, process, FAQ, contact. Websites and AI explain that kind of work, then the same three contact actions. Contact is the three links plus the short form.

The visitor’s job is to recognize the company and choose a direction: AI and LLM work, an individual website, enterprise software, or something else.

## Layout

- The first viewport states what NisCorp AI does and shows the three directions.
- Mobile-first. On a narrow viewport the header, the three cards, and the floating button remain usable. The button does not cover those actions.
- Type scale, alignment, and spacing should make the page look composed and current. A wall of equal body text is a failed layout.
- Off-white ground, near-black text, one accent on emphasis and the primary path. WhatsApp green only on the WhatsApp control.
- Tailwind is the styling system. Keep tokens few: background, text, accent, and the WhatsApp color.

## Interaction

Phone is a `tel:` link. Email is a `mailto:` link. WhatsApp is `https://wa.me/<E.164 without plus>?text=...`, including the floating button. The form does not post. Submit opens WhatsApp with name, path, and message. A second action opens that text in the email app.

## Leave out

Dark mode, a component library, counters, logo bars, carousels, pricing tables, placeholder portfolios, and decoration that does not help the visitor choose.
